# CQ-05 · frame-not-depicted
#
# Question: Does any document in the corpus depict a Frame — that is, does
#           `vso:depicts` anywhere reach the lens instead of the world?
# Persona:  P1 — generation-pipeline engineer. Clause C9 is the one that keeps
#           the camera out of the object list a renderer is handed.
# Spec:     docs/vson.md §2 clause C9; §3.1 (Frame is not an Entity)
# Form:     ASK — a conformant corpus answers false
# Note:     The five Frame subtypes are named explicitly because the corpus
#           carries no TBox and this pack runs under no entailment regime: an
#           asserted `a vso:CameraView` does not yield `a vso:Frame` here.
#           Gallery scenes 13–15 attach Negation, BeliefState and Quantification
#           nodes with `vso:depicts`; those are reification nodes, not Frames,
#           and C9 does not reach them (`vss:DepictsEntityShape`, §5.2).
PREFIX vso: <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/ontology#>

ASK {
  ?scene  vso:depicts ?target .
  ?target a ?kind .
  VALUES ?kind {
    vso:Frame vso:SceneContext vso:VisualStyle
    vso:CameraView vso:Composition vso:Persona
  }
}
